    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IAtr">I Atr</ref> 1.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="216" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf he ðonne tyhtbysig sy, gange to þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þryfealdan ordale.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="216" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IAtr_1-1.lnote.oe.7"/> he ðonne tyhtbysig sy, gange<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IAtr_1-1.lnote.oe.9"/> to ðam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IAtr_1-1.lnote.oe.10"/> ðreofealdan ordale.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="217" ed="#liebermann"/>Si tyhtbisi sit (id est accusationibus infamatus), ad triplex ordalium uadat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="1.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="52" ed="#robertson"/>Gyf he ðonne tyhtbysig sy, gange to ðam ðreofealdan ordale.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IAtr_1-1.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="217" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IAtr_1-1.lnote.de.2"/> [Angeklagt]er nun oft bescholten ist, gehe er zum dreifachen Ordal.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IAtr_1-1.lnote.de.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If the [accused] is then of bad repute, let him go to the threefold ordeal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IAtr_1-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="53" ed="#robertson"/>If, however, he is of bad reputation, he shall go to the triple ordeal.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="217"><ref target="clause:IIIAtr_3-4">III Atr 3.4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. III Atr. 3, 4</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIIAtr_3-4">III Atr 3.4</ref>; <ref target="clause:IICn_22">II Cn 22</ref>; <ref target="clause:IICn_30">II Cn 30</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_30">II Cn 30</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 30: I Atr 1:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="367"><label>parallel</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_30-1">II Cn 30.1</ref> <quote>I Atr 1:1,4/II Cn 30:1,3,3a</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares III Atr 3, 4.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IAtr_1-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">216</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IAtr_1-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">216</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gang <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gang Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IAtr_1-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">216</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IAtr_1-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">147</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hier sollte neues Kapitel beginnen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">A new chapter should begin here</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IAtr_1-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">147</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das Folgende, ausser 1, 14. 3, nimmt II Cn 30—33 (= Hn 65, 3) auf, mit absichtlicher Änderung; Ordal (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 22ff. 33a) fordert Cnut für einfache Reinigung überhaupt nicht (II 22 = Hn 64, 9) und dreifaches nur gegen 3 Kläger: letzteres vielleicht nur Begriffsverdeutlichung zu ‘bescholten’; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3. 5a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">What follows, except 1, 14. 3, is taken up by II Cn 30—33 (= Hn 65, 3), with deliberate alteration; Cnut does not require ordeal (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 22ff. 33a) at all for simple exculpation (II 22 = Hn 64, 9), and requires the triple ordeal only against 3 accusers: the latter perhaps merely clarifies the concept ‘of ill repute’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3. 5a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IAtr_1-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">147</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu diesem Falle kehrt 1, 4 zurück, nachdem in 1, 2; 3 eine Ausnahme davon behandelt ist</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">1, 4 returns to this case, after an exception to it has been dealt with in 1, 2; 3</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IAtr_1-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">312</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and those following cf. II Cn. 30–3.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
